    },
    {
      "text": "The system shall limit the maximum speed at which Autopilot can be engaged to 85 mph (or the posted speed limit, whichever is lower) and shall automatically deactivate if the vehicle exceeds this limit."
    },
    {
      "text": "The system shall continuously perform health‑monitoring of all primary sensors (camera, radar, ultrasonic) and shall prevent Autopilot activation or automatically disengage if any sensor is degraded, obstructed, or provides inconsistent data."
    },
    {
      "text": "The system shall provide redundant, cross‑checked perception pathways (e.g., radar‑camera fusion) to maintain lane‑keeping and collision‑avoidance capabilities in the event of a single‑sensor failure."
    },
    {
      "text": "The system shall detect and correctly handle missing, faded, or ambiguous lane markings by either alerting the driver and disengaging Autosteer or by safely transitioning to a minimal‑assistance mode."
    },
    {
      "text": "The system shall monitor driver attention using an eye‑tracking or head‑pose sensor and shall issue escalating warnings, followed by Autopilot disengagement, if driver gaze is not directed toward the forward roadway for more than 2 seconds."
    },
    {
      "text": "The system shall ensure that Forward Collision Warning (FCW) and Automatic Emergency Braking (AEB) remain fully functional and can override Autosteer commands to apply maximum safe braking when an imminent collision is detected."
    },
    {
      "text": "The system shall only allow activation of Autopilot on roadways that meet predefined criteria (e.g., limited‑access highway, clear lane markings, visibility > 500 m) and shall refuse activation on roads that do not satisfy these conditions."
    },
    {
      "text": "The system shall record a secure, tamper‑evident log of all sensor inputs, system decisions, driver interventions, and disengagement events, and retain this data for at least 30 days for post‑incident analysis."
    },
    {
      "text": "The system shall perform a self‑test on power‑up and before each Autopilot activation, verifying that all critical software modules, sensor calibrations, and communication links are within nominal parameters, and shall abort activation if any test fails."
